{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793815743,"nonce":"Calzn7jqfCUvdaKTUjY5AH2s1aA=","title":"git work pull adds the tracker's fetch refspecs to the remote's config","message":"The tracker's remote-tracking refs live at `refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/work-*/\u003cid\u003e`. Under the default refspec `+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/*`, git reads them as branches. `git remote prune` and `git fetch --prune` map them back to `refs/heads/work-*`, find nothing there, and delete all of them. The next `git work pull` fetches everything again, so a branch-sync script that prunes and `git work sync` keep undoing each other. Nothing is lost, but every run re-fetches the whole tracker.\n\nThe fix today is manual (README, quickstart): add `+refs/\u003cns\u003e/*:refs/remotes/\u003cremote\u003e/\u003cns\u003e/*` to `remote.\u003cremote\u003e.fetch` for each of the four namespaces. Prune then maps the refs back to their real source and removes only refs that were actually deleted on the remote. Tested: go-git accepts these refspecs. A negative refspec (`^refs/heads/work-*`) also stops the pruning, but go-git rejects it (`malformed refspec, separators are wrong`) and git-work stops working, so that route is out.\n\nThis manual step goes against this story's outcome (no hand-editing git config). `git work pull` (and so `sync`) should add any missing refspecs to the remote it pulls from, via the git CLI (`gitcli`), and say once that it did. Once it ships, the README and quickstart notes shrink to a single line.\n\nSeparately: `entity/dag/entity.go:80` (`readRemote`) builds `refs/remotes/\u003cnamespace\u003e/\u003cremote\u003e/\u003cid\u003e`, which has the namespace and remote swapped. It appears to have no callers; fix or delete it.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["core"],"parent":"bc14d4d88d377f01d8cdafffc35fa0ee11b5b4795ec8034742de3e1cc15858ac","priority":"medium","status":"to-do","type":"task"}}]}